<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 20px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Intelligent Robots – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Grade:</b> 11th Grade (CEFR: B1.2)</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Scenario:</b> Intelligent Robots</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Theme:</b> How Technology Changes Society</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="2"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Give a simple, prepared presentation on current events or past experiences. Interactive: Participate in debates on issues of general interest, current or historical.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can give a simple presentation about the future impact of artificial intelligence by expressing hypothetical outcomes (e.g., "If AI continues to evolve, it might change the job market significantly.")</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can participate in debates, responding to arguments and agreeing or disagreeing with respect and clarity (e.g., "It is agreed that AI could create jobs, but new skills may also be required.")</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can conduct interviews about AI and technology, asking open questions (e.g., "How do you think Panama's logistics and trade industries could change with AI integration in the future?")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 35%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #333; width: 15%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a series of images showing different applications of AI and robots (e.g., self-driving cars, robotic surgery, AI in customer service, smart homes). Students are asked to call out what they see and say one word about how it affects society. The teacher then asks open-ended questions like, "What kind of intelligent robots have you heard about recently?" or "How do you think technology has already started to revolutionize our daily lives?" (5 min)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models sentences using conditional forms to predict future impacts, such as, "If AI continues to advance, it might drastically change the job market." and "AI systems are programmed to learn from data." The teacher pays special attention to the pronunciation of the long vowel sound /ɑː/ in words like "robot," "job," and "start," as well as the alternation of full and reduced vowels in multisyllabic words like "innovative" and "technological." (5 min)</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of key terms and structures. For instance, after modeling a conditional sentence, the teacher asks: "Does 'If AI continues to advance, it might drastically change the job market' mean this will definitely happen, or is it a possibility?" (Expected answer: "A possibility.") "When we say 'AI systems are programmed,' does the AI do the programming itself?" (Expected answer: "No, people program it."). (3 min)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio clip (2-3 minutes) of an expert interview discussing potential societal changes due to AI and intelligent robots, focusing on future opportunities and challenges in different sectors. The interview includes phrases using conditional forms, future simple, and passive voice. For example, "If AI is integrated into healthcare, patient experiences will be enhanced," or "New employment opportunities might be created, but existing job markets could also shift."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> The students will be able to identify main ideas and specific details about predictions and potential impacts of AI on society from an expert discussion, preparing them to form their own opinions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist questions:</b> "What is the main topic of the interview?" (Expected answer: "The future impact of AI on society.") "What are the two main areas of discussion?" (Expected answer: "Opportunities and challenges.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False statements:</b> Students listen and mark T or F for statements like "AI will only create new jobs, never replace old ones." (F) or "The expert believes AI could enhance customer service significantly." (T).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Students match phrases from the interview with their predicted outcomes (e.g., "AI integration in logistics" to "Improved efficiency").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Speaking)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice using conditional forms (e.g., "If AI continues to evolve, it might change the job market significantly."), Future simple (e.g., "AI will create new employment opportunities."), and Passive voice (e.g., "AI systems are programmed to learn from data and perform tasks.") to express predictions and discuss hypothetical outcomes related to the theme. Key vocabulary: advance, evolve, revolutionize, adapt, create, enhance, job markets, employment, opportunities, challenges, functionality.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice – Sentence Completion & Oral Repetition:</b> The teacher provides sentence stems on the board or a handout that students complete orally in pairs, using the target grammar and vocabulary. E.g., "If AI ____ (verb: advance/evolve), it ____ (verb: revolutionize/enhance) ____ (noun: customer service/job markets)." "AI systems ____ (passive voice: are programmed/will be updated) to ____ (verb: learn/perform)." Students repeat their complete sentences, focusing on pronunciation. (5 min)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice – Prediction Dominoes:</b> Students work in small groups. Each group receives a set of "dominoes" where one half has an "if" clause (e.g., "If AI becomes more intelligent...") and the other half has a "result" clause or phrase (e.g., "...new careers will be established." or "...societal challenges might arise."). They must orally connect the dominoes to form logical conditional sentences, expanding on the ideas aloud. E.g., "If AI becomes more intelligent, new careers will be established, and people will need to adapt their skills." (5 min)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction – Hypothetical Interview:</b> Students interview each other about specific hypothetical AI impacts in Panama, using open questions. For example, "How do you think Panama's logistics and trade industries could change with AI integration in the future?" or "If AI becomes widespread, what specific challenges do you predict for employment in Panama?" They practice asking thoughtful questions and responding with clarity. Peer check: One student listens for correct use of conditional forms and specific vocabulary, while the other focuses on pronunciation. (7 min)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">17 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative task:</b> "The Future Impact Panel Discussion"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Description:</b> Students form groups of 4-5 to conduct a mini-panel discussion or debate on the future impact of AI and intelligent robots on society, specifically focusing on job markets and daily life. Each student takes on the role of an expert or concerned citizen with a particular perspective (e.g., technology enthusiast, labor union representative, ethicist, entrepreneur). They must express hypothetical outcomes using conditional forms, predict future trends with the future simple, and discuss how AI systems are "programmed" or "developed" using the passive voice.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Groups receive a scenario question (e.g., "What will be the most significant change in daily life if AI becomes completely integrated into smart cities?").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students take 2 minutes to prepare their initial statement, outlining their perspective and using at least one conditional sentence and one future simple prediction.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each 'expert' presents their opening statement (1 minute per person).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Follow-up discussion: Students respond to each other's arguments, agreeing or disagreeing respectfully. E.g., "It is agreed that AI could create jobs, but new skills may also be required," or "While I understand your point about challenges, if these systems are responsibly programmed, we might see more opportunities."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher circulates, offering support, encouraging participation, and noting use of target language.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency, collaborative interaction, expressing predictions, responding to arguments, and using sociolinguistic competence by asking about technology thoughtfully and discussing its societal role sensitively.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist. The teacher will use a checklist to assess individual and group performance during the panel discussion, focusing on specific speaking criteria.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students participate actively in the "Future Impact Panel Discussion," giving a simple presentation of their perspective and engaging in a debate, expressing hypothetical outcomes and responding to arguments.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear articulation of words, especially those with /ɑː/ and attention to vowel reduction in multisyllabic words (e.g., "innovative," "technological").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Integration of at least 5-7 words from the provided list (e.g., artificial intelligence, job markets, opportunities, challenges, evolve, revolutionize, adapt, enhance).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Accurate use of grammar:</b> Correct application of conditional forms (e.g., "If... might/will"), future simple, and passive voice.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and coherence:</b> Arguments and predictions are clear, logical, and easy to follow.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaborative interaction:</b> Active listening, respectful responses, and engaging meaningfully with peers' points.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete an exit ticket with the following prompts:</p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One new idea I learned about the future impact of AI is..."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"One conditional sentence I used effectively today was..."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of discussing the future of intelligent robots did I find most challenging, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can I improve my ability to express predictions and respond to arguments in English?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Did students successfully use conditional forms and future simple to express hypothetical outcomes and predictions? Were specific vocabulary terms related to AI and technology consistently used?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Was the panel discussion engaging and did it encourage active, respectful interaction among students? What adjustments might be needed to encourage more balanced participation or deeper critical thinking in future speaking tasks?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can this speaking practice be leveraged for the next lesson (Lesson 4: Writing Composition), especially in structuring arguments or presenting future scenarios in written form?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> This lesson's focus on expressing predictions and arguments orally about AI's societal impact will directly prepare students for Lesson 4 (Writing Composition), where they will construct written paragraphs and essays detailing their perspectives on these same topics, using the practiced grammar and vocabulary.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>